# Running the app ("run" shortcut)

When the user writes just **"run"** (or "run it" / "start the app"), start BOTH servers
in the background and confirm they are healthy. Do not ask for more detail.

## Steps

1. Free the ports if something is already listening (avoid "port in use"):
   - backend: stop any `python.exe` whose command line contains `uvicorn`
   - frontend: stop any `node.exe` whose command line contains `next`
2. Start the backend (Python venv, port 8000):

```powershell
cd "c:\Users\jachy\Desktop\Vysoká\práce\cursor\hackaton\backend"
.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m uvicorn app.main:app --port 8000
```

3. Start the frontend (Node, port 3000):

```powershell
cd "c:\Users\jachy\Desktop\Vysoká\práce\cursor\hackaton\frontend"
npm run dev
```

4. Verify and report the URLs:
   - backend health: `GET http://127.0.0.1:8000/health` should be `{"status":"ok", ...}`
   - frontend: `http://localhost:3000` should return 200

## Notes

- Both run as long-lived background processes; the backend has NO auto-reload, so
  after editing `backend/.env` or backend code it must be restarted.
- The backend reads `backend/.env` (`LLM_BASE_URL`, `LLM_MODEL`, `LLM_API_KEY`).
  Without a key it runs in mock LLM mode; nothing breaks.
- App URL to open: http://localhost:3000
